WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:08.076
Dyson is known for revolutionizing the vacuum. Sir&nbsp;
James Dyson hoped to create another revolutionary product -&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.076 --> 00:00:14.160
an electric car to compete with Tesla. The&nbsp;
Dyson car was supposed to be on the road in 2021&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:21.197
but then the project got axed. Constructing cars&nbsp;
at any scale takes blood, sweat, tears, and even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.197 --> 00:00:30.437
more money. It was too expensive to build. Dyson had&nbsp;
a legacy to protect. So does Sony. The Japanese tech&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.437 --> 00:00:35.840
giant is one of the most recognized brands in the&nbsp;
world, famous for the PlayStation and the Walkman -&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:42.700
if you're old enough to remember it. But no one saw&nbsp;
this coming. Sony took almost everyone by surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:49.103
by unveiling an electric car at the 2020 Consumer&nbsp;
Electronics Show in Las Vegas. This wasn't just a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.103 --> 00:00:56.732
concept, this was a prototype. The car is drivable.&nbsp;
The team that built Aibo, Sony's cute robotic dog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.732 --> 00:01:00.722
built the car with the help of the renowned&nbsp;
Magna Steyr which manufactures vehicles like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.722 --> 00:01:06.673
the Mercedes-Benz G-Class. This car is called&nbsp;
the Vision-S, Sony's vision for the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.673 --> 00:01:14.273
Mobile has been the mega trend of the last&nbsp;
decade. I believe the next mega trend will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:21.202
mobility. Mobility is defined as fundamentally&nbsp;
changing the way we travel. A car won't just be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.202 --> 00:01:27.120
a way to get from point a to point b. It's a piece&nbsp;
of technology, an iPhone on wheels. The vehicle will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:32.534
be connected to the internet. It knows the location&nbsp;
of the person it's picking up while the passenger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:38.378
can also follow the car along its route. The Sony&nbsp;
car is jam-packed with Sony stuff. Touch screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.378 --> 00:01:45.040
panoramic Sony displays filled with Sony-owned&nbsp;
movies and music. Each seat has its own speakers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.880
so you wouldn't need to fight over what music to listen to. And if you're listening through your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.312
earbuds before getting into the car, Sony envisions&nbsp;
the music automatically transferring to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.312 --> 00:01:59.680
vehicle's speakers. The idea is to make the ride as&nbsp;
comfortable as time spent in your own living room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.640
with the understanding that one day, there&nbsp;
won't even be a driver. Cars will be autonomous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.103
Sony's is not yet fully autonomous but it is&nbsp;
moving in that direction thanks to a whopping 33&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.103 --> 00:02:16.240
sensors located both inside and outside. According&nbsp;
to the company, the autonomy level of Vision-S&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.440
is two or greater. The driver is still in control&nbsp;
but the vehicle is aware of its surroundings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.080
It can recognize when other obstacles are in&nbsp;
its way before parking and knows when to change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.360
lanes while keeping a safe distance from other vehicles. Sensors can even read the driver's facial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:37.040
expressions to gauge levels of concentration and fatigue and send out alerts if necessary. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.584
temperature will be automatically adjusted&nbsp;
to match the comfort level of people inside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.200
Sony originally said it had no intention of&nbsp;
mass producing the car. The prototype was simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:53.280
developed to show off its technology. But plans may have changed. After its unveiling in Las Vegas,&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:58.240
the car moved to Magna Steyr's engineering&nbsp;
facility in Graz, Austria for fine tuning.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:03.920
And then in July, Sony announced it would begin&nbsp;
testing the car on roads in Japan. This suggests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.640
the company may have bigger plans for the Vision-S
than simply to advance the sensing and audio

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.926
technology for other carmakers to use in their vehicles. It does already dabble in the auto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:19.187
industry by supplying image sensors to companies&nbsp;
like Toyota to help with automatic emergency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.187 --> 00:03:24.862
braking. Sony hopes software updates will move its&nbsp;
car up to at least level four which means the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.862 --> 00:03:30.924
vehicle does all the driving but only in a limited area. The highest level is full self-driving.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.841 --> 00:03:38.067
The car performs all tasks under all circumstances.&nbsp;
It's the same level Tesla aims to achieve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:44.320
Elon Musk's company has completely turned the auto industry upside down.Other electric cars are often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:50.400
compared to a Tesla. So how does the Vision-S&nbsp;
stack up against Tesla's mass-market Model 3?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:56.400
Depending on the version of the Model 3,&nbsp;
it can go 0 to 60 mph in 3.1 to 5.3 seconds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:02.566
Sony claims its car can accelerate in 4.8&nbsp;seconds.
The top speed of the Tesla ranges from 140&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.566 --> 00:04:12.000
to 162 mph compared to Sony's 149 mph. The&nbsp;
Model 3 has a driving range of 267 to 360 miles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:17.056
We don't yet know how far Sony's car can go nor&nbsp;
do we know what price it would be if it does go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:22.179
on sale one day. If it's more expensive than the&nbsp;
Model 3 and a comparison with the Model S is more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.179 --> 00:04:26.080
appropriate, it does lag behind in acceleration&nbsp;
and speed. &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:32.399
A big difference between the two companies is&nbsp;
that Sony relies on LiDAR to advance its self-driving technology

00:04:32.399 --> 00:04:37.252
LiDAR is a sensor that helps detect objects by&nbsp;
beaming out laser light and then measuring the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.252 --> 00:04:42.928
the time it takes for the light to reflect back. Musk&nbsp;
once called LiDAR a fool's errand and said anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.928 --> 00:04:49.280
relying on the expensive sensor is doomed. Instead,&nbsp;
Tesla uses a combination of cameras, radar, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:54.976
ultrasonics to see. LiDAR is very popular with tech companies other than Tesla. It's found in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.976 --> 00:05:00.871
Apple's iPhone 12 Pro to help take better photos. And, by the way, Apple is also reportedly wading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.871 --> 00:05:06.557
into the car market. Rumors of an Apple electric car have run rampant for years. It even hired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.557 --> 00:05:12.400
a bunch of engineers from Tesla but its efforts have been&nbsp;
shaky from the start with leadership changes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:18.607
hundreds of layoffs from the car division a couple of years ago. Apple's&nbsp;direction has reportedly shifted to developing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.607 --> 00:05:24.000
an autonomous driving system rather than a&nbsp;
complete car but who knows what the future holds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.254 --> 00:05:29.943
Apple's challenges show just how difficult it&nbsp;
can be even for well-established companies to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.943 --> 00:05:36.244
build electric cars. Dyson learned that the hard way. But the difficulty doesn't appear to deter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.244 --> 00:05:42.962
Sony. We are excited about the road ahead of us. It will be a long road ahead. 

00:05:42.962 --> 00:05:50.055
If Sony does end up producing&nbsp;&nbsp;a car for the masses, be prepared to wait because&nbsp;autonomous cars need to clock in a lot of hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.055 --> 00:05:54.812
in order to gather enough driving data. Although&nbsp;
Sony hasn't provided many updates about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.812 --> 00:06:01.007
development of its car, all the pieces of the&nbsp;
puzzle seem to point to more than just a prototype.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.203 --> 00:06:05.067
I'm Cindy Pom, thanks for watching. If you like&nbsp;
what you saw, give it a like and don't forget to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:10.367
subscribe to my channel. And thank you very much to my Patrons for your support. I'll see you next week.

